  "description": "Three-phase energy meter for DIN rail or panel with TCD current sensors: voltages, currents, powers, power factors, frequency, energies, demand and setup",
  "revision": 1,
  "source": "Carlo Gavazzi, EM210_AV Communication Protocol, version 4 revision 3",
  "sources": [
    {
      "title": "EM210_AV Communication Protocol",
      "version": "version 4 revision 3",
      "url": "https://www.gavazziautomation.com/fileadmin/images/PIM/OTHERSTUFF/COMPRO/EM210_CP.pdf",
      "accessed": "2026-11-14",
      "sha256": "b1edeb5732c21bf32abf938c3848f3a4b247fca45b0e4551f35f0dbc5cd51dbc",
      "note": "register tables read from the manufacturer's document"
    }
  ],
  "notes": [
    "Modbus RTU over RS485. Functions 03h and 04h read the same registers; 06h and 10h write. Up to 125 registers per read.",
    "Addresses are the physical addresses of the manual (the 3xxxxx Modicon numbers less 300001).",
    "32-bit and 64-bit values, floats included, have the least significant word first; bytes in a word are MSB first.",
    "The PFA and PFB (MID) models implement a subset: the registers marked so are missing on them (EM210 PFA/PFB communication protocol, version 4 revision 3, https://www.gavazziautomation.com/fileadmin/images/PIM/OTHERSTUFF/COMPRO/EM210_MID_CP.pdf).",
    "Written from the manufacturer's document; not tested on a device."
  ],
  "protocol": "rtu",
  "byte_order": "big",
  "word_order": "little",
  "address_base": 0,
  "x_status": "official",
